==Trivia==
*In the Japanese version, the Energy Drink's equivalent is the '''Masculinity of Kyushu''' (九州の男らしさ), Kyushu being the largest of Japan's islands.
**The Masculinity of Kyushu appears to be a ''fundoshi'' (a traditional Japanese loincloth that fell out of use after World War II but can still be seen during a [[wikipedia:Hadaka Matsuri|Hadaka Matsuri]]) with the kanji 男 (''otoko'', meaning "man") on it.
**In the [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|original English version]], its name was shortened to just '''Masculinity'''.
*The name of the Treasure is slightly inaccurate, as three cans are shown, making the correct alias "Energy Drinks".
*The label of the Energy Drinks resembles the real-life drink brand [[wikipedia:Monster Energy|Monster Energy]].
*It is the only Treasure set to have its own [[Catnip Challenges|Catnip Challenge]].
